<p>Use this menu to make basic print settings.</p>
<p>Available functions differ depending on the printer or printer driver you are using.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="default" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Restore Defaults</span></p>
<p>Restores the settings on this menu to the default settings.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="orient" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Orientation</span></p>
<p>Select the orientation of your document.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="colorbw" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Color/ Black and White:</span></p>
<p>Select whether the document is printed in color or black and white.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Color images will be printed using CMYK toner: 
 Cyan, Magenta, Yellow, and Black. CMY are the three primary subtractive 
 colors.</p></li>
<li><p>If you want to adjust the print color, use the 
 settings on the <span class="Term-Soft">Print Quality:Standard</span> and/or 
 <span class="Term-Soft">Print Quality:Advanced</span> menus.</p></li>
<li><p>For two-color printing, select <span class="Term-Soft">Color</span>. 
 Configure two-color printing in the <span class="Term-Soft">Two-color:</span> 
 list on the <span class="Term-Soft">Print Quality:Standard</span> menu.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="rotated" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Rotate by 180 Degrees</span></p>
<p>Prints the image upside down.</p>
<p>For example, use this function if paper loaded in a tray has the top 
 and bottom fixed, and printing with the paper in that direction would 
 otherwise make the image upside-down.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="copies" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Copies:</span></p>
<p>Enter the number of copies. Depending on the printer you use, the maximum 
 number of copies may be different.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="docusize" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Document Size:</span></p>
<p>Select the paper size set in the application. Most applications will 
 specify the paper size automatically, so this setting might not be necessary. 
 To specify a non-standard paper size, select a registered custom paper 
 size. Alternatively, enter the paper size in the <span class="Term-Soft">Custom 
 Paper Size</span> dialog box, which is accessible through <span class="Term-Soft">Custom 
 Paper Size...</span>.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>If you select a document size conflicting with 
 the size set in your application, the document may be printed with the 
 one specified in the application.</p></li>
<li><p><span class="Term-Soft">Custom Paper Size 1</span> 
 to <span class="Term-Soft">Custom Paper Size 10</span> can be registered 
 on the <span class="Term-Soft">Advanced Options</span> tab in the printer 
 properties dialog box. Depending on the printer you are using, up to 100 
 custom paper sizes can be registered.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="custom" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Custom Paper Size...</span></p>
<p>Opens the <span class="Term-Soft">Custom Paper Size</span> dialog box, 
 where you can specify a non-standard paper size.</p>
<p><a href="~/Topics/idh_how_custom">Printing on Custom Size Paper</a></p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="reduce" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Reduce/Enlarge:</span></p>
<p>You can reduce or enlarge the image.</p>
<p><a href="~/Topics/idh_how_zoom">Reducing and Enlarging a Document Size</a></p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Off</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Do not reduce or enlarge the image.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Fit to Print Size</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">The document is automatically reduced or enlarged 
 to fit the paper size selected in the <span class="Term-Soft">Print On:</span> 
 list.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Zoom</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Select it if you want to reduce or enlarge the image 
 manually.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Directional Magnification</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Enter reduction and enlargement ratios for the vertical 
 and horizontal directions separately.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="zoom" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Zoom:</span></p>
<p>When you want to zoom in or out the image to print, define the value 
 in % in the spin box. The original size of the document is able to shrink 
 or enlarge from 25% to 400% when printed.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>This function is available only if <span class="Term-Soft">Zoom</span> 
 is selected for <span class="Term-Soft">Reduce/Enlarge:</span>.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="magnification" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Vertical:</span> / <span class="Term-Soft">Horizontal:</span></p>
<p>Enter reduction and enlargement ratios for the vertical and horizontal 
 directions separately by specifying a percentage between 25 and 400% (adjustable 
 in steps of 1%).</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="printon" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Print On:</span></p>
<p>When you want to print the document on a different size paper than the 
 document size specified in the <span class="Term-Soft">Document Size:</span> 
 list, select the physical paper size from the list. If you do not want 
 to change the print size, you may select <span class="Term-Soft">Same as 
 Original Size</span>.</p>
